From 904bb979f178ed0f99d78812fdb3433c28a7f352 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MaxiRazorback <344630105+MaxiRazorback@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 18:12:53 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] FSR-201..209: temporal FSR 3.1 and Intel XeSS from the 0020
 scene inputs

- Temporal FSR 3.1 (FidelityFX API) and Intel XeSS-SR use patch 0020's
  scene capture (colour, depth, motion vectors, jitter) on the default
  renderer; fsr_upscaler (fsr3, fsr4, xess) picks the backend and
  version, fsr_temporal turns it on.
- upscale_ratio sets the render size below the output (1, 1.3 ... 3;
  0 follows the window).
- The window title names the upscaler in use (ryty_upscaler_status.h).
- Depth reaches FSR/XeSS through an R32 copy; the reconstruction is
  blitted to the native image (AMD faulted on D32S8 views and the view
  copy draw).
- DIAG-206: VK_EXT_device_fault report on device loss.
- XeSS needs libxess.dll next to GTSport.exe; headers in xess_api.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
